+## A build plan shows its code
+
+Every step in a build plan carries the code it will write, as a diff under
+`docs/plans/<feature>-code/`, shown by `make_page.py` plan mode (#469, #473). Each step opens with
+one plain sentence per change, then one captioned block of code per change, with line numbers and
+no mid-word wrapping; tests are folded under their names. The builder refuses a draft that breaks
+a readable-code rule (`scripts/readability.py`, the house standard in
+`rules/standards/coding-philosophy.md`), so the user never reads code that hasn't been made
+readable. The user ticks Looks right on each step; the copy box holds the approval only when every
+step is ticked, and an edit on the page comes back as changed lines that I apply to the draft.
